  "subtitle": "Commuter-specific effects of segregated cycle infrastructure on bike-share use in Glasgow · MSc Urban Analytics, University of Glasgow",
  "intro": "Does segregated cycle infrastructure get more people on bikes? I modelled {summary.trips} nextbike trips between 11,060 pairs of Glasgow docking stations. On <b>commuter corridors</b>, a fully segregated route carries about <b>3.3x the trips</b> of one with none (95% CI 2.0 to 5.5), the only infrastructure effect that held up under robust clustering. The catch: the median commuter route is only 10% segregated.",
